      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While anecdotal advice online is common, you need a more targeted approach than just high-dose Vitamin C. Instead of just flushing, try making dietary changes to reduce oxalate intake, which is the actual stone-forming culprit. For serious prevention, a comprehensive diet plan alongside increased water intake is more effective than just boosting one vitamin. Please consult a registered dietitian who specializes in kidney health to create a safe and effective prevention strategy.",
      "source": "target",
